The DUT is a failing rising-edge detector. The correct implementation: pulse <= din & ~previous; previous <= din.

Let me write it properly.

Interface: module rising_edge(input clk, rst, din, output reg pulse);

Note the interface says width 1 for all ports. The current module uses implicit port declarations which is fine but let me be explicit.

One consideration: pulse should be combinational? No — spec says "All state updates on rising clk", so pulse is registered. Output pulse becomes din AND NOT previous sampled din. Yes registered.

Let me write:

module rising_edge(
  input logic clk,
  input logic rst,
  input logic din,
  output logic pulse
);
  logic previous;
  always_ff @(posedge clk) begin
    if (rst) begin
      previous <= 1'b0;
      pulse <= 1'b0;
    end else begin
      pulse <= din & ~previous;
      previous <= din;
    end
  end
endmodule

That's correct. Use always_ff. Fine for synthesis.

